// Regression fixture for final-review Critical 1 (memory-audit-4e
// whole-branch review, probe P5): an element of one global container read
// into another global. Originally (4e): `cl_free_globals` had no runtime-
// aliasing analysis, so it always froze both `p5Gl` (element-freeing its
// one stored handle) and `p5GSaved` (freeing the very same handle again):
// SIGSEGV. The globals escape pre-pass fixed the crash by disqualifying
// both from `cl_free_globals`.
//
// ARC Task 4 (counted named-slot stores): `p5GSaved = p5Gl[0]` is a
// NAMED-SLOT store (global) whose source is a non-birth list-index read
// (`EIndexRef`, a raw borrow -- see p4_elem_escape.cla's own comment for
// why that's different from a map subscript) -- `lowCountedStore` retains
// it FIRST, then releases `p5GSaved`'s OLD (default-empty) handle
// (confirmed against the emitted C: `rt_text_retain(cv___store1);
// rt_text_release(cv_p5GSaved); cv_p5GSaved = cv___store1;`).
//
// ARC Task 5 (counted container element slots) DELETED the old
// index-read-disqualifies-the-container consult -- `p5Gl` is no longer
// disqualified by `p5GSaved = p5Gl[0]`'s own read at all, and (unlike
// `p5GSaved`) nothing ELSE in this fixture disqualifies it either (`p5Gl`'s
// own push source, `"x"+"y"`, is a fresh concat -- rule 2 never fires), so
// `p5Gl` now QUALIFIES for `cl_free_globals`'s real, deep release --
// confirmed against the emitted C: `cl_free_globals` now contains `{
// int32_t i; for (...) rt_text_release(*(rt_text **)rt_list_at(cv_p5Gl,
// i)); } rt_list_release(cv_p5Gl);`. Safe: the element it walks is `p5Gl`'s
// OWN reference to the shared "xy" text (rc==2, since `p5GSaved`'s own read
// retained independently above), so the walk's release only drops rc to 1,
// never to 0.
//
// Through Task 5, `p5GSaved` itself stayed globally-unqualified for the
// SAME orthogonal rule p4_elem_escape.cla's own updated comment explains in
// full (rule 4: a bare-identifier LHS reassigned from a rhs -- `p5Gl[0]`,
// an ExIndex -- `lowEscapeFreshInit` doesn't recognize as fresh; untouched
// by Task 5).
//
// ARC Task 6 (globals release unconditionally) makes that rule moot too:
// `cl_free_globals` no longer consults `lowGlobalsVarQualifies`, so
// `p5GSaved` is released along with `p5Gl` now (confirmed against the
// emitted C: `cl_free_globals` gains `rt_text_release(cv_p5GSaved);` after
// `p5Gl`'s own deep-release block). Expected strict-mode leak count: 0
// (../p5_global_elem_alias.leaks deleted -- was 2). Safe: the shared "xy"
// text's rc==2 (one from `p5Gl`'s own retained element, one from
// `p5GSaved`'s retain-at-store) is drained back to 0 by the two
// independent releases, in declaration order (`p5Gl` first, `p5GSaved`
// second) -- neither side ever touches the other's +1.

var p5Gl: list of text
var p5GSaved: text

func runP5GlobalElemAlias() {
    p5Gl.push("x" + "y")
    p5GSaved = p5Gl[0]
    alert("p5 done")
}
